  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 226 PM CDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nMore mild conditions are expected through the end of the work week \nwith highs in the upper 70s and 80s across the state. Continued \nridging out to our south and west will continue, but there is decent \nsignal for more shortwaves Wednesday into Thursday that could bring \nin additional chances for showers and storms. Severe weather is less \nlikely with these storm chances, as moisture will be limited, but \nmore details will be sorted out in the coming days. The ridge is \nagain expected to intensify over the central plains during the \nweekend and heat will likely return by Saturday and Sunday. \nContinued NW flow could bring in a marginal chances for smoke \nhaze since wildfires are still ongoing in Canada.",
